Station H-07 in survey area H presents a six-layer resistivity profile. The sequence starts with a very high resistivity surface layer (1790.5 ohm-m), dropping sharply to 73.0 ohm-m at a depth of 24.85 m. Resistivity then rises to 540.2 ohm-m at layer 5 before declining slightly to 520.8 ohm-m in layer 6.

The on-file classification of QHAA is inaccurate. The actual resistivity transitions result in a QHAK curve type, as the final triplet (layers 4, 5, and 6) follows a K-type pattern (103.4 < 540.2 > 520.8).

{"curve_type_stated": "QHAA", "label_issue_flagged": true}

